{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\n\nRaymond III was born around 1140. His father Raymond II was a powerful nobleman in the Kingdom of Jerusalem and had been appointed as the regent of the kingdom by King Baldwin III. After the death of Raymond II in 1152 Raymond III succeeded him as Count of Tripoli.\n\nRaymond III played an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem during the reign of King Amalric I. He was a close ally of the king and participated in several military campaigns against the Fatimid Caliphate. In 1164 Raymond III was captured by the forces of Nur ad-Din during the Battle of Harim.\n\n*Capture and Imprisonment*\n\nRaymond III was imprisoned for several years by Nur ad-Din. During his imprisonment Raymond III was forced to witness the execution of several of his fellow Christian prisoners. He was eventually ransomed and released in 1173.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\n\nAfter his release from prison Raymond III returned to Tripoli and resumed his role as Count. He continued to play an important role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and participated in several military campaigns against the forces of Saladin. Raymond III died in 1187 during the Siege of Tripoli.\n\nRaymond III was succeeded as Count of Tripoli by his nephew Raymond IV. He was remembered as a brave and loyal nobleman who played an important role in the defense of the Kingdom of Jerusalem against the forces of Islam.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004263356793671846}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35265472531318665}, {"token": " of",